{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:42489485 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:42489485 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"42489485","source":"MED","pmid":"42489485","pmcid":"PMC13463774","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC13463774"]},"doi":"10.1128/mbio.01295-26","title":"AlphaFold-driven structural proteomics reveals extensive cellulosome machinery in human ruminococcal symbionts.","authorString":"Minor C, Takayesu A, Arbing MA, Ha SM, Gunsalus RP, Pellegrini M, Sawaya MR, Clubb RT.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Minor C","lastName":"Minor","firstName":"Christine","initials":"C","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0005-5342-3917"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."},{"affiliation":"UCLA-DOE Institute of Genomics and Proteomics, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Takayesu A","lastName":"Takayesu","firstName":"Allen","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."},{"affiliation":"UCLA-DOE Institute of Genomics and Proteomics, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Arbing MA","lastName":"Arbing","firstName":"Mark A","initials":"MA","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"UCLA-DOE Institute of Genomics and Proteomics, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."},{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Chemistry, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Ha SM","lastName":"Ha","firstName":"Sung Min","initials":"SM","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Integrative Biology and Physiology, University of California Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Gunsalus RP","lastName":"Gunsalus","firstName":"Robert P","initials":"RP","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1937-8412"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"UCLA-DOE Institute of Genomics and Proteomics, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."},{"affiliation":"Department of Microbiology, Immunology, and Molecular Genetics, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Pellegrini M","lastName":"Pellegrini","firstName":"Matteo","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"UCLA-DOE Institute of Genomics and Proteomics, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."},{"affiliation":"Department of Molecular, Cell, and Developmental Biology, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Sawaya MR","lastName":"Sawaya","firstName":"Michael R","initials":"MR","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0874-9043"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."},{"affiliation":"UCLA-DOE Institute of Genomics and Proteomics, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."},{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Chemistry, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."},{"affiliation":"Molecular Biology Institute, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Clubb RT","lastName":"Clubb","firstName":"Robert T","initials":"RT","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5718-3985"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."},{"affiliation":"UCLA-DOE Institute of Genomics and Proteomics, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."},{"affiliation":"Molecular Biology Institute, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5718-3985"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1937-8412"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0874-9043"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0005-5342-3917"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"8","volume":"17","journalIssueId":4242640,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Aug","monthOfPublication":8,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"mBio","title":"mBio","essn":"2150-7511","issn":"2150-7511","nlmid":"101519231","isoabbreviation":"mBio"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-08-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"e0129526","abstractText":"Cellulosomes are large, surface-displayed enzyme complexes that enable anaerobic bacteria to degrade recalcitrant plant polysaccharides, yet cellulosome-expressing bacteria are thought to be rare in the human gut. Here, we show that extensive sequence divergence obscures the detection of many ruminococcal cellulosomes by conventional sequence homology-based methods. Using proteome-scale AlphaFold2 structural predictions, we uncovered a substantially expanded set of putative cellulosome-producing <i>Ruminococcus</i> species, including six previously unrecognized human symbionts. Structure-based clustering identifies several novel cohesin families that retain conserved folds despite extreme sequence divergence and define distinct, phylogenetically conserved cellulosome architectures. The analysis reveals <i>R. callidus</i> and related human symbionts encode elaborate cellulosomes that are invisible to sequence-based annotation. Similarly, <i>R. difficilis</i>, a human gut symbiont, has been found to possess genes for an atypical cohesin-based assembly enriched in amylases and related starch-binding proteins, which may enable this microbe to degrade resistant starches that evade digestion in the upper gastrointestinal tract. Together, these findings reveal that ruminococcal cellulosomes are far more prevalent and diverse than previously appreciated and demonstrate the power of structural proteomics to uncover deeply divergent functional systems in the gut microbiome.IMPORTANCEPlant cell wall polysaccharides are a major dietary carbon source, yet their degradation relies on rare, highly specialized microbial enzyme assemblies known as cellulosomes, which have long been considered uncommon in the human gut. Using proteome-scale structure prediction combined with experimental validation, we show that cellulosomes are far more widespread and structurally diverse in human-associated <i>Ruminococcus</i> species than previously appreciated. We identify multiple new cohesin families and reveal distinct cellulosome architectures likely adapted to degrade different dietary substrates. Together, these findings redefine the distribution and evolution of cellulosomes in gut microbes and demonstrate the power of structural proteomics to uncover deeply diverged biological systems.","affiliation":"Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry, University of California, Los Angeles, Los Angeles, California, USA.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","grantId":"T32 GM145388","orderIn":0},{"agency":"U.S. Department of Energy (DOE)","grantId":"DE-FC02-02ER63421","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIH HHS","acronym":"OD","grantId":"S10 OD021527","orderIn":0},{"agency":"U.S. Department of Energy","grantId":"DE-FC02-02ER63421","orderIn":0},{"agency":"HHS | National Institutes of Health (NIH)","grantId":"T32GM145388","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Institutes of Health","grantId":"R01-AI161828","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","grantId":"P30 GM124165","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIAID NIH HHS","acronym":"AI","grantId":"R01 AI161828","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIH HHS","acronym":"NH","grantId":"R01-AI161828","orderIn":0},{"agency":"HHS | National Institutes of Health","grantId":"T32GM145388","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Cellulosomes","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Ruminococcus","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CY","qualifierName":"cytology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"IP","qualifierName":"isolation & purification"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cellulose","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Bacterial Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Proteomics","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Phylogeny"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Symbiosis"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Amino Acid Sequence"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Protein Conformation"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Gastrointestinal Microbiome"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Cohesins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Ruminococcus","Cellulosome","Structural Proteomics","Human Gut","Alphafold"]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Cellulose","registryNumber":"9004-34-6"},{"name":"Bacterial Proteins","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"cohesins","registryNumber":"0"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/mbio.01295-26"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13463774"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13463774?pdf=render"}]},"commentCorrectionList":{"commentCorrection":[{"source":"PPR","id":"PPR1224913","type":"Preprint in","note":"Link created based on a title-first author match","orderIn":10002}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["gca","pfam","pdb"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2026-08-17","dateOfCreation":"2026-07-23","dateOfRevision":"2026-08-17","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-07-23","firstPublicationDate":"2026-07-23","firstIndexDate":"2026-07-23","fullTextReceivedDate":"2026-09-09","hasEvaluations":"N"}]}}